    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` lookup table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `getTimezone()` getter that maps the existing `getLocality()` region to its IANA name (returning `null` when the region isn't in the table).\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.getTimezone()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.timezone` by name.\n\nThe derivation reuses the same region logic already used for `locality` (postcode-preferred, with city-table fallback), so `timezone` stays consistent with the reported region. The new `Cp42Tests` and all 56 existing tests pass.",
